## 📋 MANUAL RESEARCH — SCHEDULE, now evidence-backed

**Log the TOP BRACKET only, at three passes:**

| Pass | Band |
|---|---|
| **10:30–11:00 AM ET** | **58–69¢** |
| **12:00 PM ET** | **58–69¢** |
| **4:00 PM ET** | **58–79¢** |

All prices are **ASK**, not mid. You pay the ask. An earlier sweep done on mid
overstated the 55–59 band by 1–2 points and produced numbers that did not
reproduce — if two analyses of this data ever disagree, check which price they
used first.

### ⚠️ THE FLOOR IS 58, NOT 60 — corrected 2026-08-30

Splitting the 50s revealed the earlier "55–59 doesn't work" conclusion was
averaging two different populations. 10am–1pm ET, ask price:

| band | n | win% | avg ask | P&L |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 55–57 | 246 | 53.7% | 56.0¢ | **−2.38** |
| **58–59** | **174** | **64.9%** | **58.5¢** | **+6.44** |
| **60–64** | **392** | **68.6%** | **61.9¢** | **+6.69** |

**58–59 behaves like 60–64, not like 55–57.** +6.44 vs +6.69 — statistically
indistinguishable, on samples of 174 and 392. Meanwhile 55–57 is clearly
negative on 246 observations, so this is not a thin-cell artifact.

Confirmed independently at 4pm ET: 55–57 −2.09, everything ≥58 positive. **The
58 line holds at both times of day**, which makes it far more credible than a
single cut would be.

Moving the floor from 60 to 58 adds roughly 30% more opportunities with no
measurable loss of edge.

### The ceiling is ~69 in the morning, ~79 in the afternoon

Checked whether the ceiling is soft the way the floor was. 10:00–12:30 ET:

| band | n | win% | P&L |
|---|---|---|---|
| **58–69** | **597** | **72.9%** | **+10.16** |
| 70 | 31 | 71.0% | +0.97 |
| 71–72 | 45 | 80.0% | +8.62 |
| 73–79 | 117 | 73.5% | −2.20 |
| 80+ | 57 | 84.2% | −2.60 |

**Do not extend the morning ceiling.** 71–72 looks good but sits between +0.97
and −2.20 on cells of 31–45. Adjacent cent-wide bands swinging break-even →
+8.62 → negative is what happens when 250 observations get sliced into pieces of
30. Contrast the 58 finding, which had a clean shape on 174/392/246. **58–69 is
the largest cell in the table at n=597 and the answer.**

**The morning/afternoon asymmetry is real:** in the morning the 70s are dead or
noisy; at 4pm the 70s are the BEST band (+7.33, n=260). A 74¢ favorite at 10:30
is priced on a forecast; at 4pm it is priced on a high that has already happened.

### The other finding: the BAND, not the minute

60–69¢ was positive at **10 of 11 hours** and at **all twelve 15-minute slices**
tested between 10am and 1pm:

10:00 +4.62 · 10:15 +9.09 · 10:30 **+16.93** · 10:45 +14.19 · 11:00 +10.80 ·
11:15 +7.53 · 11:30 +12.89 · 11:45 +13.85 · 12:00 +12.18 · 12:15 +9.05 ·
12:30 +6.59 · 12:45 +6.67

**The ordering is noise.** 10:00 is the worst cell and 10:30 the best, thirty
minutes apart. Cells are ~80 correlated observations. An earlier read that "noon
beats 12:45 because of the cost-of-certainty curve" did NOT survive — the same
four-point decline inside the noon hour does not appear inside the 10am or 11am
hours. Average across all twelve is ~+10¢. **Pick a time that fits the day.**

### A BAND, never an open-ended floor

Open-ended floors all fail because they drag in the 80+ tier, which wins 85–96%
and pays nothing at 87–94¢:

| floor | negative at |
|---|---|
| 50c+ | 7 of 11 hours |
| 55c+ | 6 of 11 hours |
| 60c+ | 7 of 11 hours |

**Screen 58–69, not "58 and over."** The ceiling matters as much as the floor.

### The afternoon trend — the most convincing pattern found

| ET | 60–69 | 70–79 | 70–79 win% |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2pm | −0.42 | −6.99 | 66.7% |
| 3pm | +0.50 | +3.88 | 78.2% |
| 4pm | +4.38 | +6.36 | 80.6% |
| 5pm | +7.17 | **+10.41** | 84.6% |

**Win rate climbs 66.7% → 84.6% while the price stays flat near 74¢.** The market
fails to reprice as certainty increases — a cleaner structural signal than
anything in the morning cells, because it is a consistent trend across eight
cells rather than one good number.

5pm is best; **4pm gives up ~4¢ for a workable hour**; 3pm is where it thins out.

At 4pm the full band breakdown: 55–57 −2.09 (n=54), 58–59 +21.40 (n=50),
60–69 +6.48 (n=242), 70–79 +7.33 (n=260). **Discount that 58–59 number** — 80%
win at 58.6¢ is out of line with both neighbours and is what 50 observations
produce by chance. "58–59 works," not "58–59 is triple the others."

### Per-city (12:45 ET, 60c+, before the ceiling was established)

Positive: San Antonio +25.47, Austin +22.79, LAX +18.38, OKC +17.43, Vegas
+14.56, Phoenix +6.70, Dallas +5.13, Miami +3.13, NY +0.76, Philadelphia +0.50.
